{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1450929-differentiating-between-anima-mundi-and-hisil-inhabitants","id":1450929,"title":"Differentiating between Anima Mundi and Hisil inhabitants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-04T01:46:38-07:00","id":1450929,"title":"Differentiating between Anima Mundi and Hisil inhabitants","content":"Hello everyone:<br /> <br /> This question comes from Mage the Awakening 2nd Ed mostly. The inhabitants of the Shadow are spirits, ephemeral beings of instinct and feelings. You can have the spirit of a stray dog, or the spirit of all stray dogs, or even the spirit of feeling stranded. The Anima Mundi contains the collective ideas about stuff, so you could also have a goetia of stray dogs or feeling stranded, which feels quite redundant, even if they would be two different entities. Am I interpreting the type of inhabitants for each realm correctly? How could I make them more distinct from each other?<br /> <br /> Thank you!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26646-zanchito","name":"Zanchito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T02:28:22-07:00","id":1450935,"title":"","content":"On my phone, so the links aren\u2019t pretty, but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774948-subtle-differences-between-goetia-and-spirits\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774948-subtle-differences-between-goetia-and-spirits\"> Subtle Differences between Goetia and Spirits - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774948-subtle-differences-between-goetia-and-spirits\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774948-subtle-differences-between-goetia-and-spirits </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So, a thing I was thinking about after re-reading Astral Realms and everything related to the Shadow. Obviously, a Spirit is entirely divorced from human thought and perception; as far as I'm aware, even low-Rank Goetics are quite capable of complex thought that a Spirit would need to be Rank 3 at least to approach human thought processes in terms of breadth. The main thing I'm wondering is, if you put a Spirit of Fire and a Goetia of Fire side-by-side, how could you tell the difference between them without resorting to Mage Sight? Side note: What is the relationship between the Anima Mundi and the </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1383870-what-is-the-difference-in-behavior-between-spirits-and-goetia\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1383870-what-is-the-difference-in-behavior-between-spirits-and-goetia\"> What is the difference in behavior between Spirits and Goetia? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1383870-what-is-the-difference-in-behavior-between-spirits-and-goetia\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1383870-what-is-the-difference-in-behavior-between-spirits-and-goetia </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Since they can have overlapping influences like fear or hope, and thanks to the deepest parts of the Astral maybe even Goetia of the concept hunt, prey and maybe even animals. How would spirits and goetia of the same influence act different? If i have mages with Spirit and Mind why would they choose the help of one or another of these types of beings? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> These should help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T02:55:38-07:00","id":1450936,"title":"","content":"Anima Mundi has no care at all about human ideas or concepts so there wouldn't even be anima mundi goetia of things like feeling stranded to begin with. It'd have dog goetia, far bigger than most dog spirits (because dog spirits are dog sized), but human culture stuff isn't a part of it and it wouldn't be influenced by needing to constantly devour essence to survive. / get changed by what they eat. It is just &quot;Dog&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T07:15:44-07:00","id":1450955,"title":"","content":"Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26646-zanchito","name":"Zanchito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}